WEBVTT


00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.540
I was in Korea last week and these are some differences that I noticed

00:00:02.541 --> 00:00:04.141
as someone living in Japan currently.

00:00:04.142 --> 00:00:05.541
First in the tourist areas of Seoul,

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:07.541
I feel like their English was really really good.

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:09.501
I definitely tried to prepare a little bit of Korean.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:11.661
I don't speak Korean but I wanted to learn basic things

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:13.581
but for the most part I didn't have to use like any Korean

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.781
because everyone spoke really good English

00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:15.861
whereas here in Japan

00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:18.481
I feel like good English speakers are a lot harder to come by.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.660
Um, thankfully I speak half Japanese but yeah,

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:21.861
that was one big thing I noticed.

00:00:21.862 --> 00:00:22.541
The second thing I noticed,

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:24.261
I think there's a lot of foreigner and

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:25.861
tourist fatigue in both countries

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:28.501
but I did feel it a little bit more in Seoul.

00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:30.101
Like I feel like when I walked into the store

00:00:30.102 --> 00:00:31.741
the clerks weren't as like

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:34.261
openly friendly and didn't do as much like

00:00:34.262 --> 00:00:35.901
over the top customer service things

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.461
whereas here in Japan definitely like

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:41.421
go out of their way to be very attentive and have like

00:00:41.422 --> 00:00:42.301
really good customer service

00:00:42.302 --> 00:00:44.141
for in my experience. No. 3,

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.301
this is just my opinion but I thought Korean train stations

00:00:46.302 --> 00:00:48.261
were a little easier to navigate than Japanese train station.

00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:48.821
This could also be

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:51.481
because I already have experience with Japanese train stations

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.820
like they're not that different

00:00:52.821 --> 00:00:54.701
but when I first went to Japan

00:00:54.702 --> 00:00:57.821
I definitely got lost especially like big train stations like Shinjuku,

00:00:57.822 --> 00:00:59.661
Shibuya, etcetera.

00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:02.781
Whereas like even at Seoul Station in Korea,

00:01:02.782 --> 00:01:03.421
it was totally fine.

00:01:03.422 --> 00:01:05.501
Like I got from point a to point B in like 2 seconds.

00:01:05.502 --> 00:01:07.301
The maps were very straightforward.

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:08.221
Nothing was confusing at all.

00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:10.541
Like I never got lost trying to find my exit in Korea,

00:01:10.542 --> 00:01:12.181
whereas I've gotten lost plenty of times

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:14.321
trying to find my exit at Japanese train stations.
